"""SQLite projection, selector, and local V4.8A evidence authority.

This isolated correctness store keeps canonical records, their receipt chain,
typed observation/provenance projections, and bounded selector proofs in one
SQLite database. V3 identities are consumed as immutable inputs; no V3 schema
or ledger is modified here. The selector does not expose model, execution,
paper-trading, or live-authority APIs.

The implementation is intentionally conservative:

* one serialized writer uses ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE``;
* an operational projection binds one-shot to the governed transport clock
  and uses one exact sample for every timestamp generated by a transaction;
* an operational caller may bind every transaction to a mutable application
  fence in addition to its kernel lease; unbound use remains reference-only;
* every mutating public operation has deterministic idempotency;
* projection tables are ``STRICT`` and reject ``UPDATE``/``DELETE``;
* each disposition extends one continuous per-scope RFC 9162 tree;
* a cutoff is admitted only after explicit, gap-free, exact-one coverage;
* selection uses dual receipt/availability cutoffs and completed UTC-grid bars;
* SQL results must equal an independent canonical-record replay before commit;
* V4.3 health is reduced from causal evidence and checked against canonical
  replay; callers cannot assert ``HEALTHY``;
* the local physical gate binds an exact InformationSet, V4 selection proofs,
  decision health, and current health under one receipt snapshot;
* ``verify()`` replays operational deployment authority, receipts, typed state,
  trees, cutoffs, health, selection, and every gate verdict and ordered
  commitment from genesis.

The store is not a signed checkpoint, rollback-resistant archive, portable
range proof, governance-ledger authority bridge, order outbox, or
remote-exchange transaction. It verifies and stores an operator-installed
deployment root, but this local projection alone is not an external trust-root
anchor. Its gate is deliberately non-activating.
"""

